{"content":[{"c":["DISHAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Chieftain in the land of Seir, a mountainous area southwest of the Dead Sea. Dishan’s father was Seir the Horite (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.21","r":"Gen.36.21","rawR":"Gen.36.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.21","value":"Gen.36.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 36:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.38","r":"1Chr.1.38","rawR":"1Chr.1.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.38","value":"1Chr.1.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:38"},"). The Horites were driven out of their territory by the Edomites (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.2.12","r":"Deut.2.12","rawR":"Deut.2.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.2.12","value":"Deut.2.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 2:12"},"). Later OT references often use Seir and Edom synonymously."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Dishan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 36:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.36.21","rawQueryValue":"Gen.36.21","sourceRefExact":"Gen.36.21"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.38","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.38","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.38"},{"anchorText":"Dt 2:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.2.12","rawQueryValue":"Deut.2.12","sourceRefExact":"Deut.2.12"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"db202eac501a7be93d129ffbcec3a3ae5654a005d9321506ad6de7cba8485811","sourceItemName":"Dishan","sourceItemOrder":131,"sourceMember":"Articles/D.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Dishan","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Dishan","title":"Dishan","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}